          "source_quote": "ἵνα περὶ παντὸς οὗ ἂν χειροτονήσῃ ἐπὶ γῆς ἔσται δεδογματισμένον ἐν οὐρανοῖς",
          "english_quote": "so that whatever he determines on earth will stand decreed in the heavens",
          "issue": "The main rendering suppresses περὶ, ‘concerning’, and conceals the recurrence of χειροτονέω, rendered earlier as ‘ordain’. The Greek frames the heavenly decree as concerning the person or matter affected by Clement’s action; the English directly identifies whatever he determines with what stands decreed. The notes correctly disclose the possible personal referent, but that disclosure does not restore the wording relationship in the main text. Neither the personal nor the impersonal interpretation should be certified as uniquely established.",
          "suggested_revision": "Restore ‘concerning’ and explicitly compare a source-transparent rendering such as ‘so that concerning whatever he ordains on earth, it will stand decreed in the heavens’ with the personal alternative ‘so that concerning anyone he appoints on earth, it will stand decreed in the heavens’. Preserve the alternative interpretation in the notes and maintain a visible connection with the earlier χειροτονῶ. These are provisional candidates requiring fresh review, not accepted replacements.",
